The easy class in [S] are Valk and Barb (as in Vanilla), but also Monks.
The easier race is undoubfully the doppelganger but it's not that easy  
playing them (you need a bit of learning to use the #youpoly at full".  
Monks are better for doppelganger because they have more power (needed for  
polymorph).

Use everything the game gives you. Blessed geno ? Yes. Artifact wishes ?  
Yes. Elbereth ? Yes. self poly, polypile ? Yes. Nothing is "cheap" in your  
first ascencion, it's hard enough that way without trying a pacifist  
extinctionist foodless atheist at first...

Launch a game in explore mode. Nor only will you not die, but also get a  
WoW for starting. Then try and play it as a real game. You will learn what  
the dungeon look like, learn your quest by heart and know whether you are  
prepared for it or not, ...

Use savescumming for learning purpose. Do not use savescumming on regular  
basis, this will prevent you from learning anything. However, when you  
encounter a strange and delicate situation not met so often, do it:
Save. Copy your save. Relaunch the game and consider it as a puzzle. How  
to beat that strange situation. Try several thing, you can restore your  
game after that. Maybe even try it in explore mode to test several  
possibilities. Quit these savescummed games as soon as you have beaten the  
particular point. Then, once you have decided your course of action (might  
be flying away), get back the original save, destroy any backup you had  
(general savescumming is bad, the game is about "win or die trying") and  
go for it. Typical situations for that would be reaching the quest, Medusa  
or other special levels. That might teach you whether you are sufficiently  
equiped for that level or not.

Read all nethack and slash'em spoilers. Not all before playing, but play  
with them available (I usually play [S] with three browser tab on  
steelypics, Eva's nethack page and Eva's Slash'em page). Every time you  
get items, double check their special use (alchemy, confuse scrolls, use  
of gain level...) Read the general strategy spoilers severals times until  
you think they do not contain anything but the obvious.

