The match is not between the DL and your XL, but between your XL and your  
AC.
Around XL 8, real baddies such as ants, or q start to appears. You need to  
be prepared *before* they appear. That mean low AC, weapons, offensive  
wands, ... So don't raise your level too soon. Let your pet do the  
killing. Learn how to efficiently use pat, both for kill (still kill a few  
yourself for the HP gain, around XL 5 usually starts to feel confortable)  
or for shop robbing. Leashes and magic whistles are your best friends  
after your pet. Early potion of gain level best use is often to #dip one  
of the guard's whistle in it (so you need to let your pet level up so he  
can kill them).

Pet don't really have XP and they can 1 XP for each kill, be it a newt or  
a dragon. So learn which monster give fewer XP (newt, jackal give 1) and  
let your pet kill them. Keep the higher XP monsters (lichen is 4 XP) for  
you, in the very early game reaching XL 4-5 can be good for survival. Also  
use them (especially lichen) for weapon training. Low level monsters have  
ridiculously small attacks so they are good trainee while you should keep  
to the weapon with which you hit often for big nasty things (of course,  
being a monk greatly simplify this part).

